# aur.list — AUR packages, installed via the helper (paru) bootstrapped in
# phase 10. One per line; # comments and blanks ignored. Keep this short: every
# entry is a from-source build, so only put here what the official repos lack.
#
# No theme-settings GUI here (e.g. nwg-look): theme/icon/cursor/accent are owned
# end-to-end by the Quickshell Settings app (scripts/colorscheme.sh writes the
# GTK/Qt/KDE config). One place to manage everything — no extra app.
oh-my-posh-bin             # shell prompt engine; themes in dotfiles/oh-my-posh/
mpvpaper                   # video wallpapers (wallpaper.sh's video backend) — AUR-only, was
                           # wrongly in common.list where the pacman batch tripped over it
# gnome-network-displays (Cast to TV) is NOT here since 0.44: the Cast plugin (ewe.cast)
# `requires` it with ewe-cast, and Komble installs both with the plugin. [ewe] still
# serves it prebuilt (ewe-repo aur-packages.txt).
# mpv-uosc-git left with mpv as the video app (0.44): ewe Player plays video now.
libreswan               # IPsec for networkmanager-l2tp (L2TP/IPsec VPNs). Replaces strongswan: strongSwan 6.1
                        # disabled IKEv1 at build time and Arch ships it that way, and L2TP/IPsec IS IKEv1
                        # (Windows RRAS, MikroTik, every ISP box) — so no L2TP profile could connect
                        # (2026-09-10, "IKE version 1 not supported"). libreswan 5 keeps IKEv1 behind
                        # `ikev1-policy=accept` in /etc/ipsec.conf, which phase 30 sets. Conflicts with
                        # strongswan — phase 20 removes that first. Not in the official repos.
